# tree16_nonblocking_200Gbps.topo
# Scale-out fabric variant: all 16 hosts on ONE non-blocking switch (Podsize==
# Nodes==Radix_Down => 1 ToR, every pair one hop, no oversubscription). Identical
# to tree16_nonblocking_100Gbps.topo but the per-host link is 200 Gbps instead of
# 100. Used for the inter-node-bandwidth = 200 Gbps variant of the intranode
# link-speed sweep: at 200 the scale-out NIC (-linkspeed 200000) and this fabric
# pipe match exactly (effective = min = 200 Gbps, no NIC/fabric mismatch), so the
# only difference vs the 100 Gbps run is the inter-node bandwidth.
Nodes 16
Tiers 2
Podsize 16

Tier 0
Downlink_speed_Gbps 200
Radix_Down 16
Radix_Up 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 1
Switch_Latency_ns 0
Oversubscribed 16

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 200
Radix_Down 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 1
Switch_Latency_ns 0
